<h3 id="sc-fees">Scottish curling fees (2026-27)</h3>

<p>
  Scottish curling is the governing body of the sport in Scotland and is seeking
  registration of all players. Membership is compulsory for all club members.
</p>
<p>
  Note: Letham Grange membership fee includes the Scottish Curling fee costs.
</p>
<div class="fees-grid">
  <!-- Grid Headers -->
  <div class="fee-header"><p>Membership Category</p></div>
  <div class="fee-header numeric"><p>Fee</p></div>

  <!-- Row 1 -->
  <div class="fee-category"><p>Adult</p></div>
  <div class="fee-cost"><p>£34</p></div>

  <!-- Row 2 -->
  <div class="fee-category">
    <p>Junior - 21</p>
  </div>
  <div class="fee-cost"><p>£17</p></div>

  <!-- Row 3 -->
  <div class="fee-category"><p>Gateway</p></div>
  <div class="fee-cost"><p>£17</p></div>

  <!-- Row 4 -->
  <div class="fee-category"><p>Gateway Junior</p></div>
  <div class="fee-cost"><p>£8.50</p></div>
</div>

<h3 id="curl-forfar">Curl Forfar information</h3>
<!-- Automatically catches your balanced typography layout rules -->
<p>Forfar Indoor Sports, Carseview Road, Forfar, DD8 3BT. Tel. 01307 468668</p>

<ul class="prose-list">
  <li>
    <strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:Admin@fis.scot">Admin@fis.scot</a>
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://fis.scot">www.fis.scot</a>. Also
    on Facebook and Twitter.
    <span class="list-note"
      >[Note: FIS App for iPhone/iPad and Android phones now available]</span
    >
  </li>
  <li><strong>Catering:</strong> For bar or meals contact Sandra Ferguson</li>
  <li>
    <strong>Session times:</strong> Evening 6.00pm and 8.30pm; Weekend 11.30am,
    2.00pm and 4.30pm
  </li>
  <li><strong>Additional Bookings:</strong> Contact the rink directly</li>
  <li>
    <strong>Social events:</strong> See
    <a href="https://fis.scot">FIS website</a>
  </li>
</ul>

<h3 id="lgcc-info">Letham Grange Curling Club information</h3>
<ul class="prose-list">
  <li>Club leagues - Bank of Scotland, Contractors Cup, Spring League.</li>
  <li>
    Club Bonspiels – Pairs, Doubles, Opening, New Year, Closing, Crichton and
    Men vs Women.
  </li>
  <li>Points – All members and friends welcome</li>
</ul>
<p>
  The club is also heavily involved with the Province, Area and Ice Rink
  competitions such as;
</p>
<ul class="prose-list">
  <li>Dewar KO; Ferburn League; Points; and Indoor and/or Outdoor Bonspiel.</li>
  <li>
    Indoor Bonspiel; Grant Trophy; Crichton Tankard; Inter Province Bonspiel.
  </li>
  <li>
    Super League, Agricar League; Seniors League; Bonspiels for Opening, Closing
    and Charity; Inter Club matches; Rink Points.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  Province, Area and Ice Rink competition dates and events are in our yearly
  syllabus.
</p>

<p>The club also runs many social events such as:-</p>
<ul class="prose-list">
  <li>Fun days – Meeting up for a social event like bowling.</li>
  <li>Away days – Playing at other ice rinks in national competitions</li>
  <li>
    Dinners – Attend dinners when visiting tour come to Forfar. Dinner as part
    of our Prizegiving.
  </li>
  <li>Prize ceremonies – Annual presentation of prizes</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="volunteers">Volunteers</h3>

<p>
  Letham Grange Curling Club is self funded and run by the members volunteering
  to being on the Committee. We are always grateful for assistance in running
  the club from any of its members and especially from the parents/carers of new
  junior members. This could involve anything from lifts to competitions , to
  being on the committee or becoming a coach or official.
</p>
<p>
  If you are interested in volunteering please contact the President or
  Secretary:-
</p>
<ul class="prose-list">
  <li>President - Dave Piggot Contact- president@lethamgrangecc.org.uk</li>
  <li>Secretary - Brian McArtney Contact- secretary@lethamgrangecc.org.uk</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="cwp">Child wellbeing and protection</h3>

<p>
  Letham Grange Curling Club adheres to the highest standards of child wellbeing
  and protection, adhering to the Child wellbeing protection policy set out by
  Scottish curling . All our coaches and helpers have undergone PVG checks and
  the club has its own Child wellbeing protection officer:
</p>
<p>CWPO - Jane McArtney Contact - wellbeing@lethamgrangecc.org.uk</p>

